' F14 -- Trust boundaries: three client-facing walls and the backend wall.
' Chapter 5 (Implementation). Concept diagram. Pinned revision dfc20df6.
' Claim supported: a browser holding the anon key meets three database-side
' boundaries (table RLS, function EXECUTE grants, storage policies). The
' FastAPI backend is a fourth boundary: most routes run as service_role or
' over asyncpg, bypass RLS and check ownership in Python; a few forward the
' user's JWT so RLS applies. Sources: see MANIFEST.md (F14).
@startuml f14-trust-boundaries
!include _style.iuml

skinparam nodesep 16
skinparam ranksep 34

title Trust boundaries — three client-facing walls, one backend wall

rectangle "**Browser** · untrusted\nanon key in the bundle +\nJWT from Supabase Auth:\nrole anon or authenticated" as BR #DCDCDC

rectangle "**FastAPI** · backend wall\nchecks ownership in Python\n(e.g. v4 reader, Luna)" as API #FFFFFF

rectangle "**Postgres and Storage** · enforced per role" as PG #F2F2F2 {
  rectangle "**Storage policies**\nlecture-pdfs: private\nread: lesson visibility\nwrite: lesson owner" as ST #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**EXECUTE grants**\nSECURITY DEFINER\nfunctions skip RLS;\nanon may run none" as FN #FFFFFF
  rectangle "**Table RLS** · 79 tables, RLS on all\n**P1** own rows: user_id = auth.uid()\n**P2** creator: professor_id or\n       student_owner_id = auth.uid()\n**P3** derived: enrollment join or\n       lecture_visible_to_caller()\n**P4** backend-only: service_role\n       policies only (parse_runs)" as RLS #FFFFFF
}

BR -right-> API : "/api"
BR -down-> ST : "Storage\nAPI"
BR -down-> FN : "RPC"
BR -down-> RLS : "PostgREST"
API -[#1A1A1A,dashed]down-> RLS : "most routes: service_role\nor asyncpg, RLS bypassed;\nsome forward the user JWT"

legend bottom
  Permissive policies OR-combine: a role sees the **union** of every applicable policy (20260719020000:23-28).
  No test checks a boundary through an API route: DB tests check policies and grants directly
  in Postgres; endpoint tests run on asyncpg or a fake client without RLS.
endlegend

@enduml
